# Object models each scene loads, recorded on the console. The scene gate
# loads a scene's models before the scene starts and holds a reference to each
# until the next scene loads, so objects that spawn later (the character demo
# swaps racers) find them in the game's model cache instead of reading the
# disc. A model missing here still works: it is read when an object needs it.
#
# Regenerate from a TEX_TRACE=1 log with dreamcast/record_scenes.py.
# Format: scene LEVEL ID ...   (model IDs in hex)
scene 5 017c
scene 18 017c
scene 19 017c
scene 23 0025 0026 0027 0028 0029 002a 0031 0037 007f 0091 009e 00b6 00bc 00ca 00d3 00ef 011a 0130 0132
scene 28 017c
scene 29 017c
